A||||9||Lisa 86 2m4||door locks and dew wipes...||||5||
Z||000000||Lisa 86 2m4||12-30-2000||03:34 PM||||Is everybody sick of me yet? I don't know why I thought I could or should do this work myself, maybe because I'm a college student and poor. I just got a set of doorlocks and dewwipes from the fierostore. the skins are off my door, but I can't get the old lock cylinder out!! The door lock rod hooks into a longer clip that comes from the cylinder that moves into the lock/unlock position, I can't get the rod free of the clip and the clip is so rusted that it will be unusable and the new locks did not come with this. I'm having a really hard time getting the gasket retaining clip out too. WHat am I missing?? Or is it not me, but the rust?<BR>As I'm doing this, I'm also doing the dew wipes, and I wonder should the window be up or down as I unscrew the power mirrors and the inner dew screws?  I know I ask the stupidest questions, but I'm just starting to do this stuff myself. A tuneup was cake compared to this oddballstuff!!<BR>Thanks!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||12-30-2000||06:16 PM||||Door locks are a pain in the ass. My roommate did his and he cussed the whole time! lol...there is a retaining clip around the lock part itself if I recall, and its a B1TCH to remove and install..and on top of that, it has a tendancy to fall into the bottom of the door.<BR>Outter door skin removal isnt nec. for either project.<BR>Roll down your window when replacing the dew wipes. Its another pain in the ass project. There are two screws in the middle of the dew wipes that are another B1TCH to remove! I didnt even reinstall them when I put new dews on (you'd never know either). <BR>You have taken on two of the most difficult and mostly tedious/annoying non-mechanical tasks.....have fun!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Lisa 86 2m4||12-30-2000||06:44 PM||||I'm having so much fun, you just might find my Fiero in Tampa Bay!!!  The retaining clip for my lock cylinder, both are shot! Completely rusted as is the piece of metal that the lock rod hooks into at the end of the lock cylinder. Neither AutoZone or One Stop Auto carries anything remotely close. Anybody have any idea where I can find this items?||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||12-30-2000||08:23 PM||||Lisa, put a post in the mall, I'm sure someone should have a few of those lying around.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||12-31-2000||09:24 AM||||Kickhill should probably be able to get you those. <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>www.kickhill.com/fiero.html</A> <P>BTW, a forum full of guys never gets sick of a girl posting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||varnster||12-31-2000||02:02 PM||||lisa, I did mine and the clips were shot on<BR>mine to. I went to advance auto store,(like<BR>a napa or carquest) and just got some of those snap rings kind of looks like a 'c'<BR>these work great! their about 5 cents, get<BR>a couple in case you lose one in your door.<BR>hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||12-31-2000||05:29 PM||||Turn that plastic thingy that connects the door linkage to the lock cylinder and it will release the linkage.<P>The junkyard would be another last resort to find that clip.<P>Just trying to help out another poor college student, I'm one too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Lisa 86 2m4||12-31-2000||06:49 PM||||Thanks for the info! I have seen those C rings, so I will try those. The other clip might be more of a prob.<BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Lisa 86 2m4||01-05-2001||12:10 PM||||For those who come after me, so you know it can be done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>for the door lock cylinders, it takes a lot of pushing away from you and to the left to get that dang clip out, but it can be done!  The real trick is after you put in the new cylinder, hooking that clip back on!! But I discovered a trick... I got my hand in the panel, and to the opposite side of the black plastic thing,(hand- black plastic-lock cylinder) I have a pair of pliers that have a really long handle to them and snaked them behind the black plastic so that each half of the handle was behind the clip of the lock cylinder, with the plier handles keeping the clip away from the door skin and close to the clip, it lined right up, a little bit of umpf and the clip locked in! No time at all!<BR>The dew strips, now that's another story. I have failed at making my own tool, but came pretty close, now I"m hoping to buy one. <BR>Hope this helps someone in the future!!<BR>Lisa ||||reg||1
Z||000009||KissMySSFiero||01-05-2001||07:06 PM||||hey lisa.<BR>i just replaced the locks on my car.  got them for 10 bucks from napa.  oem part too.  that was the only good thing about the whole deal.  i had to replace them because the got broke jsut before xmas when someone broke into my car.  i never had such a hard time working on any car before.  next time someone breaks into my car.  either kill me or kill them.  it is a pain in the a$$.  of course i did the first door in about 4days.  well i dont really know.  but after i got it down i knocked out the second in about 45 min.  and if i had to do it again i would say i would have done both in that time.  problem is i tried to get  the door skin off.  and found out thats another spot they tried to break in at. the corner busted off my door skin.  oh well.  cant do anything now but glue it.  now im ranting. still kinda pi$$ed about the breakin thing.  <BR>if you have any questions post it or email me.  i just got done last night so its still fresh in my mind.  good luck<BR><P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE  88FORMULA<BR>KissMySSFiero@netzero.net<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">  <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||10
